15 U.S. Code 1681s-2 ( b ) : Requires furnishers of information to investigate and correct inaccuracies upon notification.

Truth in Lending Act ( TILA ) : 15 U.S. Code 1666b : Billing statements must be provided in a timely manner, at least 21 days before the payment due date.

Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ) Regulations : Credit bureaus must ensure fairness, accuracy, and prompt resolution of consumer disputes.

15 U.S. Code 1681n and 1681o : Violations of these laws expose furnishers and credit bureaus to liability for both willful and negligent non-compliance.

Requested Resolution I demand the removal of the inaccurate late payment notations for XX/XX/XXXX, XX/XX/XXXX, XX/XX/XXXX, and XX/XX/XXXX, and written confirmation of the correction. 
Enclosures Included are the following documents to support my claim : Copy of my identification ( ID ). 
Proof of address. 
Copy of my Social Security card. 
Highlighted credit report showing errors. 
