ause the TEPSLF deadline has already passed '. I was confused so shared with her that I have copies of the same forms I sent to studentaid all date back to XX/XX/XXXX, way before the XX/XX/XXXX deadline on the form, so again requested to speak with a supervisor or file a complaint. I asked for information for both suggestions. Again, no supervisor was available to ask to be put on the wait list a second time with notice to call back the same day ( NADA! ). So, I filed a second complaint with the same issue with student aid today ( XX/XX/XXXX at XXXX XXXX  ) with a 15-page PDF copy of all correspondence and copies of the TEPSLF forms originally submitted. In desperation and complete exhaustion of this now 3-plus year saga, I came across your website for help and answers. I am at the point of considering reaching out to the local Congress. No one should have to work on getting a clear answer on this issue for 3 years, especially when they have spent these years consistently calling and waiting for an answer only to be told "" it ' 's still in process '' and now 'it doesn't qualify? ' The other suspicion I have is how on my student aid loan forgiveness tracker all the dates now through XX/XX/XXXX are listed, then from XXXX are listed ( and I know these dates do not qualify ) but the dates that would actually put me at 120 plus payments XXXX XXXX are not even listed ( interesting ). I just need a clear answer to what in my mind seems simple. It really hurts to see ones with loans being forgiven just under a year or two from start to finish following the same steps I have been struggling to get through for years trying to be compliant and patient, but this is too much and 3 plus years is more than valid.",,Servicer under contract with Federal Student Aid,CA,95822,,Web,2025-01-08,Untimely response,No
