4. XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Loss of Rights Upon Debt Cancellation Under federal guidelines, once an original creditor cancels a debt, they receive tax benefits and often sell the account for a fraction of its value. This means that the original creditor is made whole and no longer entitled to collect. A third party, such as Spring Oaks Capital , LLC, can not assume greater rights than the original creditor had at the time of cancellation.

